{"data":{"repository":{"pullRequest":{"reviewThreads":{"totalCount":17,"pageInfo":{"hasNextPage":false,"endCursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpK0MjAyNi0wNy0wM1QxMTowNzo0M1rOjivdWw=="},"nodes":[{"id":"PRRT_kwDODKw3uc6N7PGU","isResolved":true,"isOutdated":true,"path":"docs/release-process-deep-dive.md","line":195,"startLine":192,"originalLine":195,"originalStartLine":192,"diffSide":"RIGHT","startDiffSide":"RIGHT","subjectType":"LINE","comments":{"totalCount":2,"nodes":[{"id":"PRRC_kwDODKw3uc7Rb9_Z","databaseId":3513769945,"author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"body":"The docs snippet shows `APPLE_DEVELOPER_INSTALLER_ID` being sourced from `vars.MAC_APP_SIGNING_IDENTITY`, but the workflow currently uses `vars.APPLE_DEVELOPER_INSTALLER_ID`. This makes the deep-dive misleading for anyone trying to configure pkg signing.","createdAt":"2026-07-02T14:19:39Z","replyTo":null,"outdated":true,"path":"docs/release-process-deep-dive.md","line":195,"originalLine":195},{"id":"PRRC_kwDODKw3uc7Rr9hV","databaseId":3517962325,"author":{"login":"niik"},"body":"Good catch, fixed in 1b7da92b1 - the snippet now matches the reverted workflow (`vars.APPLE_DEVELOPER_INSTALLER_ID`).","createdAt":"2026-07-03T06:40:42Z","replyTo":{"id":"PRRC_kwDODKw3uc7Rb9_Z","databaseId":3513769945},"outdated":true,"path":"docs/release-process-deep-dive.md","line":195,"originalLine":195}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDODKw3uc6N7PGz","isResolved":true,"isOutdated":true,"path":"docs/release-process-deep-dive.md","line":230,"startLine":228,"originalLine":230,"originalStartLine":228,"diffSide":"RIGHT","startDiffSide":"RIGHT","subjectType":"LINE","comments":{"totalCount":2,"nodes":[{"id":"PRRC_kwDODKw3uc7Rb-AH","databaseId":3513769991,"author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"body":"This note claims the workflow now passes `APPLE_DEVELOPER_INSTALLER_ID: ${{ vars.MAC_APP_SIGNING_IDENTITY }}`, but the actual workflow passes `vars.APPLE_DEVELOPER_INSTALLER_ID` (see .github/workflows/deployment.yml:185). The note should be updated to match the current workflow/config surface.","createdAt":"2026-07-02T14:19:39Z","replyTo":null,"outdated":true,"path":"docs/release-process-deep-dive.md","line":230,"originalLine":230},{"id":"PRRC_kwDODKw3uc7Rr9i7","databaseId":3517962427,"author":{"login":"niik"},"body":"Fixed in ee7fd9d0e - the note now reflects that the step still passes the (unset) `vars.APPLE_DEVELOPER_INSTALLER_ID`.","createdAt":"2026-07-03T06:40:43Z","replyTo":{"id":"PRRC_kwDODKw3uc7Rb-AH","databaseId":3513769991},"outdated":true,"path":"docs/release-process-deep-dive.md","line":230,"originalLine":230}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDODKw3uc6N7PHK","isResolved":true,"isOutdated":false,"path":"script/sign","line":26,"startLine":24,"originalLine":26,"originalStartLine":24,"diffSide":"RIGHT","startDiffSide":"RIGHT","subjectType":"LINE","comments":{"totalCount":2,"nodes":[{"id":"PRRC_kwDODKw3uc7Rb-Ai","databaseId":3513770018,"author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"body":"`$KEYCHAIN` is expanded unquoted. If the keychain path ever contains spaces or glob characters, `notarytool submit` will be invoked with the wrong arguments and notarization will fail.","createdAt":"2026-07-02T14:19:40Z","replyTo":null,"outdated":false,"path":"script/sign","line":26,"originalLine":26},{"id":"PRRC_kwDODKw3uc7Rr9ki","databaseId":3517962530,"author":{"login":"niik"},"body":"Fixed in 7822e916b - `$KEYCHAIN` is now quoted.","createdAt":"2026-07-03T06:40:45Z","replyTo":{"id":"PRRC_kwDODKw3uc7Rb-Ai","databaseId":3513770018},"outdated":false,"path":"script/sign","line":26,"originalLine":26}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDODKw3uc6N7PH6","isResolved":true,"isOutdated":false,"path":"script/sign.ps1","line":6,"startLine":3,"originalLine":6,"originalStartLine":3,"diffSide":"RIGHT","startDiffSide":"RIGHT","subjectType":"LINE","comments":{"totalCount":2,"nodes":[{"id":"PRRC_kwDODKw3uc7Rb-Bg","databaseId":3513770080,"author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"body":"In PowerShell, an environment variable can be set to an empty string (\"\"), which is distinct from `$null`. This guard will not skip signing when `DO_SIGN_ARTIFACTS` is present but empty, despite the message saying \"not set\". Consider treating empty as \"off\" and exiting with an explicit success code.","createdAt":"2026-07-02T14:19:40Z","replyTo":null,"outdated":false,"path":"script/sign.ps1","line":6,"originalLine":6},{"id":"PRRC_kwDODKw3uc7Rr_BA","databaseId":3517968448,"author":{"login":"niik"},"body":"Eh, this follows the convention of the other env var checks in this file. Not going to address it","createdAt":"2026-07-03T06:42:09Z","replyTo":{"id":"PRRC_kwDODKw3uc7Rb-Bg","databaseId":3513770080},"outdated":false,"path":"script/sign.ps1","line":6,"originalLine":6}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDODKw3uc6N7PIU","isResolved":true,"isOutdated":false,"path":".github/workflows/deployment.yml","line":327,"startLine":325,"originalLine":327,"originalStartLine":325,"diffSide":"RIGHT","startDiffSide":"RIGHT","subjectType":"LINE","comments":{"totalCount":3,"nodes":[{"id":"PRRC_kwDODKw3uc7Rb-B_","databaseId":3513770111,"author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"body":"The `release` job doesn't set `timeout-minutes`, but the other jobs do. This leaves the workflow susceptible to the same kind of multi-hour hang this PR is trying to prevent (e.g., packaging or publishing steps hanging).","createdAt":"2026-07-02T14:19:40Z","replyTo":null,"outdated":false,"path":".github/workflows/deployment.yml","line":327,"originalLine":327},{"id":"PRRC_kwDODKw3uc7Rr_rV","databaseId":3517971157,"author":{"login":"niik"},"body":"The other jobs got a timeout-minutes because I observed timeouts. I haven't done so for this job so I'm not gonna bother","createdAt":"2026-07-03T06:42:47Z","replyTo":{"id":"PRRC_kwDODKw3uc7Rb-B_","databaseId":3513770111},"outdated":false,"path":".github/workflows/deployment.yml","line":327,"originalLine":327},{"id":"PRRC_kwDODKw3uc7RyxcO","databaseId":3519747854,"author":{"login":"babakks"},"body":"Yeah, let's leave the release job as is.","createdAt":"2026-07-03T12:09:35Z","replyTo":{"id":"PRRC_kwDODKw3uc7Rb-B_","databaseId":3513770111},"outdated":false,"path":".github/workflows/deployment.yml","line":327,"originalLine":327}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDODKw3uc6N7cTC","isResolved":true,"isOutdated":true,"path":".github/workflows/deployment.yml","line":null,"startLine":null,"originalLine":346,"originalStartLine":343,"diffSide":"RIGHT","startDiffSide":"RIGHT","subjectType":"LINE","comments":{"totalCount":2,"nodes":[{"id":"PRRC_kwDODKw3uc7RcP4r","databaseId":3513843243,"author":{"login":"BagToad"},"body":"💭 this is actually a private repo, so I suspect this section won't work in this state.","createdAt":"2026-07-02T14:30:01Z","replyTo":null,"outdated":true,"path":".github/workflows/deployment.yml","line":null,"originalLine":346},{"id":"PRRC_kwDODKw3uc7RrqHc","databaseId":3517882844,"author":{"login":"niik"},"body":"You're right. I believe this was broken before this change since the SITE_DEPLOY_PAT wasn't present in the staging environment either. I would like for the dry-run to be able to uncover problems with site deployment as well which but that would require us to federate the site deploy app secrets to the staging environment as well so I'm not sure we need to be able to test publishing the site in the staging environment.\r\n\r\nI'm gonna gate all the site stuff behind the production check for now","createdAt":"2026-07-03T06:25:08Z","replyTo":{"id":"PRRC_kwDODKw3uc7RcP4r","databaseId":3513843243},"outdated":true,"path":".github/workflows/deployment.yml","line":null,"originalLine":346}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDODKw3uc6OKVAz","isResolved":true,"isOutdated":true,"path":".github/workflows/deployment.yml","line":null,"startLine":null,"originalLine":23,"originalStartLine":null,"diffSide":"RIGHT","startDiffSide":null,"subjectType":"LINE","comments":{"totalCount":1,"nodes":[{"id":"PRRC_kwDODKw3uc7RwwlX","databaseId":3519220055,"author":{"login":"babakks"},"body":"**nitpick:**\n\n\n```suggestion\n        description: \"The deployment environment.\"\n```","createdAt":"2026-07-03T10:22:49Z","replyTo":null,"outdated":true,"path":".github/workflows/deployment.yml","line":null,"originalLine":23}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDODKw3uc6OKbFH","isResolved":true,"isOutdated":true,"path":".github/workflows/deployment.yml","line":null,"startLine":null,"originalLine":125,"originalStartLine":114,"diffSide":"RIGHT","startDiffSide":"RIGHT","subjectType":"LINE","comments":{"totalCount":1,"nodes":[{"id":"PRRC_kwDODKw3uc7Rw4up","databaseId":3519253417,"author":{"login":"babakks"},"body":"**nitpick:** let's quote constructed paths for consistency:\n\n\n```suggestion\n          # create a keychain for the certificate\n          PW=pwd.${{ github.run_number }}\n          security create-keychain -p $PW \"$RUNNER_TEMP/build.keychain\"\n          security set-keychain-settings -lut 21600 \"$RUNNER_TEMP/build.keychain\"\n          security default-keychain -s \"$RUNNER_TEMP/build.keychain\"\n          security unlock-keychain -p $PW \"$RUNNER_TEMP/build.keychain\"\n\n          # import the certificate\n          base64 -d <<< \"$DEVELOPER_ID_CERT\" > \"$RUNNER_TEMP/cert.p12\"\n          security import \"$RUNNER_TEMP/cert.p12\" -k \"$RUNNER_TEMP/build.keychain\" -P \"$DEVELOPER_ID_CERT_PASSWORD\" -T /usr/bin/codesign\n          security set-key-partition-list -S apple-tool:,apple:,codesign: -s -k $PW \"$RUNNER_TEMP/build.keychain\"\n          rm \"$RUNNER_TEMP/cert.p12\"\n```","createdAt":"2026-07-03T10:29:18Z","replyTo":null,"outdated":true,"path":".github/workflows/deployment.yml","line":null,"originalLine":125}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDODKw3uc6OKdd4","isResolved":true,"isOutdated":true,"path":".github/workflows/deployment.yml","line":null,"startLine":null,"originalLine":145,"originalStartLine":null,"diffSide":"RIGHT","startDiffSide":null,"subjectType":"LINE","comments":{"totalCount":1,"nodes":[{"id":"PRRC_kwDODKw3uc7Rw77r","databaseId":3519266539,"author":{"login":"babakks"},"body":"**nitpick:** the same quoting:\n\n\n```suggestion\n            --keychain \"$RUNNER_TEMP/build.keychain\"\n```","createdAt":"2026-07-03T10:32:06Z","replyTo":null,"outdated":true,"path":".github/workflows/deployment.yml","line":null,"originalLine":145}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDODKw3uc6OKffb","isResolved":false,"isOutdated":false,"path":".github/workflows/deployment.yml","line":172,"startLine":172,"originalLine":172,"originalStartLine":null,"diffSide":"RIGHT","startDiffSide":null,"subjectType":"LINE","comments":{"totalCount":1,"nodes":[{"id":"PRRC_kwDODKw3uc7Rw-r1","databaseId":3519277813,"author":{"login":"babakks"},"body":"Nice comment. 🙏 ","createdAt":"2026-07-03T10:34:13Z","replyTo":null,"outdated":false,"path":".github/workflows/deployment.yml","line":172,"originalLine":172}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDODKw3uc6OKp8q","isResolved":true,"isOutdated":true,"path":".github/workflows/deployment.yml","line":null,"startLine":null,"originalLine":398,"originalStartLine":396,"diffSide":"RIGHT","startDiffSide":"RIGHT","subjectType":"LINE","comments":{"totalCount":1,"nodes":[{"id":"PRRC_kwDODKw3uc7RxMy_","databaseId":3519335615,"author":{"login":"babakks"},"body":"With the added `if`, the `GPG_SIGN` env var will always be `true` and hence redundant. So, let's simplify this step **(together with the next suggestion):**\n\n\n```suggestion\n        if: ${{ inputs.environment == 'production' }}\n```","createdAt":"2026-07-03T10:46:03Z","replyTo":null,"outdated":true,"path":".github/workflows/deployment.yml","line":null,"originalLine":398}]}},{"id":"PRRT_kwDODKw3uc6OKqNU","isResolved":true,"isOutdated":true,"path":".github/workflows/deployment.yml","line":null,"startLine":null,"originalLine":405,"originalStartLine":null,"diffSide":"RIGHT","startDiffSide":null,"subjectType":"LINE","comments":{"totalCount":1,"nodes":[{"id":"PRRC_kwDODKw3uc7RxNKM","databaseId":3519337100,"author":{"login":"babakks"},"body":"Continued from the previous comment:\n\n```suggestion\n          gpg --yes --detach-sign --armor repodata/repomd.xml\n```"